   "text": "The ground speeds up at once; the atmosphere is pulled along only by friction, and that takes time. For the first hours, the air is left behind. At a twelve hour day, the ground is moving through the air at about four hundred and sixty meters a second, faster than the speed of sound. Winds like that would strip the surface, and they would only be the beginning."
